                ))}
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Women's Table -->
        <div class="table-panel" id="tab-women" role="tabpanel">
          <h3 class="table-heading">Women's Indian to US Shoe Size Chart</h3>
          <div class="table-wrapper">
            <table class="size-table" aria-label="Women Indian to US shoe size chart">
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>India Size (UK)</th>
                  <th>US Women Size</th>
                  <th>EU Size</th>
                  <th>Foot Length (CM)</th>
                  <th>Inches</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                {womenSizes.map(r => (
                  <tr>
                    <td class="primary-cell"><strong>India {r.india.toFixed(1)}</strong></td>
                    <td class="highlight-cell"><strong>US {r.us.toFixed(1)}</strong></td>
                    <td>EU {r.eu}</td>
                    <td>{r.cm.toFixed(1)} cm</td>
                    <td>{r.inch.toFixed(1)}"</td>
                  </tr>
                ))}
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Kids' Table -->
        <div class="table-panel" id="tab-kids" role="tabpanel">
          <h3 class="table-heading">Kids' & Youth Indian to US Shoe Size Chart</h3>
          <div class="table-wrapper">
            <table class="size-table" aria-label="Kids Indian to US shoe size chart">
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>India Kids Size</th>
                  <th>US Kids Size</th>
                  <th>EU Size</th>
                  <th>Foot Length (CM)</th>
                  <th>Age Stage</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                {kidsSizes.map(r => (
                  <tr>
                    <td class="primary-cell"><strong>India {r.india}</strong></td>
                    <td class="highlight-cell"><strong>US {r.us}</strong></td>
                    <td>EU {r.eu}</td>
                    <td>{r.cm.toFixed(1)} cm</td>
                    <td>{r.stage}</td>
                  </tr>
                ))}
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Editorial SEO Prose Section -->
    <article class="editorial-band">
      <div class="page-inner prose-article">
        <h2 class="editorial-main-title">Complete Guide to Indian Shoe Sizes and Converting to US Footwear</h2>
        
        <p class="lead-paragraph">
          If you are shopping online from American retailers like Amazon US, Nike, Nordstrom, or StockX, knowing your exact <strong>india footwear size</strong> translated into the American sizing system is critical. Sizing conventions in India have a distinctive historical origin rooted in the British imperial scale, but modern shoppers must frequently compare domestic numbers against American and European metrics. Whether you wear Bata, Red Tape, Liberty, or Mochi, this in-depth guide explains how an <strong>indian shoe size chart</strong> functions and how to convert your footwear size to US shoes with complete confidence.
        </p>

        <h3>How an Indian Shoe Size Chart Works</h3>
        <p>
          Historically, shoe manufacturing across India was standardized around the British English scale. Under this system, shoe sizes increment by one barleycorn (1/3 of an inch, or 8.46 mm) per full size, and 1/6 of an inch (4.23 mm) for half sizes. Because of this heritage, an <strong>indian size chart shoes</strong> listing is identical in length to the United Kingdom standard.
        </p>
        <p>
          Consequently, a query like <strong>uk size 8 in india</strong> refers to an Indian size 8. If an Indian shoemaker stamps an "8" on a leather oxford or casual loafer, that shoe is designed to fit a 27.0-centimetre footbed—the exact anatomical length of a UK 8 and a European 42. However, the United States system calculates numbers differently, meaning your Indian size must be converted before purchasing American sneakers or dress shoes.
        </p>

        <h3>Core Formulas: Converting Indian Shoe Sizes to US Sizes</h3>
        <p>
          Converting your domestic size from an <strong>india foot size</strong> to an American US size depends strictly on whether you are buying men's or women's footwear:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Men's Conversion (US = India + 1):</strong> American men's footwear is labeled 1 full size higher than Indian sizing. For example, if you wear an Indian size 7, your US size is 8.0 (26.0 cm, EU 41). If your Indian size is 8, you will order an American US 9.0 (27.0 cm, EU 42). If your Indian size is 9, your American size is US 10.0 (28.0 cm, EU 43).</li>
          <li><strong>Women's Conversion (US = India + 2):</strong> On an <strong>indian shoe size chart women</strong>, American women's sizes run 2 full numbers larger. If you wear an Indian size 5 in domestic sandals or pumps, your American size is US 7.0 (24.0 cm, EU 38). An Indian size 6 converts to an American US 8.0 (25.0 cm, EU 39).</li>
          <li><strong>Children's Sizing:</strong> Indian children's footwear corresponds to UK youth sizing, which is roughly 0.5 to 1 size smaller than American children's numbering (e.g., India 9.5C child equals US 10C, approximately 16.5 cm).</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Demystifying Common European Sizing Queries in India</h3>
        <p>
          Shoppers in India often encounter European numbers on multi-brand platforms like Myntra, Flipkart, Ajio, and Nykaa. Here is how popular European size searches relate to Indian and US sizing:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>36 shoe size in india:</strong> European 36 corresponds to Indian size 3 to 3.5 for women (fitting a 22.5 cm foot length), converting to an American US Women 5.5.</li>
          <li><strong>37 size in shoes in india:</strong> European 37 matches Indian size 4 to 4.5 (23.5 cm foot length), converting to an American US Women 6.5.</li>
          <li><strong>38 foot size in india & shoe size 38 in india:</strong> European 38 represents Indian size 5 for women (24.0 cm foot length), converting directly to American US Women 7.0.</li>
          <li><strong>39 eu size in india:</strong> European 39 equals Indian size 6 for women (25.0 cm foot length), which corresponds to American US Women 8.0 or US Men 6.5.</li>
          <li><strong>Shoe size 41 in india:</strong> European 41 corresponds to Indian size 7 for men (26.0 cm foot length), translating to American US Men 8.0.</li>
          <li><strong>42 foot size in india:</strong> European 42 matches Indian size 8 for men (27.0 cm foot length), which converts to American US Men 9.0.</li>
          <li><strong>43 shoe size india:</strong> European 43 equals Indian size 9 for men (28.0 cm foot length), translating to American US Men 10.0.</li>
          <li><strong>Shoe size 44 in india:</strong> European 44 represents Indian size 9.5 to 10 for men (28.5 to 29.0 cm foot length), corresponding to American US Men 10.5 to 11.0.</li>
          <li><strong>45 shoe size in india:</strong> European 45 corresponds to Indian size 10.5 to 11 for men (29.5 to 30.0 cm foot length), mapping to American US Men 11.5 to 12.0.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Foot Width and the New Indian "Bha" Sizing Standard</h3>
        <p>
          One crucial factor when converting from an Indian size to an American shoe is width. The Council of Scientific and Industrial Research - Central Leather Research Institute (CSIR-CLRI) conducted a comprehensive 3D foot scanning survey across 30 states in India. The findings demonstrated that Indian feet are on average 5% to 8% broader at the ball and forefoot than typical Western feet.
        </p>
        <p>
          To address this, the Bureau of Indian Standards (BIS) formulated the "Bha" size standard. While length follows familiar metric benchmarks, Indian lasts provide greater room across the metatarsal heads. When ordering from US brands, which default to "D" width for men and "B" width for women, individuals with broader feet often experience tightness. Choosing a "Wide" (EE for men, D for women) or sizing up by half a size ensures optimal comfort.
        </p>

        <h3>Step-by-Step: Measuring Foot Size at Home with an India Footwear Guide</h3>
        <p>
          Before ordering footwear from overseas, follow these steps to measure your foot and consult our <strong>foot size chart india</strong>:
        </p>
        <ol>
          <li>Place a blank sheet of white paper on a hard, even floor against a perpendicular wall.</li>
          <li>Stand straight with your heel lightly touching the wall. Place your full body weight on your foot, wearing your typical everyday socks.</li>
          <li>Have someone mark the furthest tip of your longest toe (which may be your big toe or second toe) with a pencil held perpendicular to the floor.</li>
          <li>Measure the distance from the wall edge of the paper to the toe mark using a millimetre ruler.</li>
